// Worked example: fillet only top-face edges via topology-relational selectors
// PRD: docs/prds/topology-selectors.md task 7
//
// Demonstrates the topology-relational selectors from §3.9: pick the single
// upward-facing face of a box, walk its adjacent faces, collect the edges shared
// with each adjacent face, and fillet only those (the four top-perimeter edges).
//
// Coverage:
//   1. faces_by_normal(solid, direction, tol) + single() → top-face selection
//   2. flat_map(adjacent_faces(solid, face), |f| shared_edges(face, f)) →
//      walk topology to collect the perimeter edges of the chosen face
//   3. fillet(solid, edges, radius) → apply the fillet to the curated edge set
//
// Capability status: LIVE. 3-arg `fillet(solid, edges, radius)` — the
// compiler stdlib binding (`crates/reify-compiler/src/geometry_modify.rs`,
// `"fillet" => match compiled_args.len() { 2 | 3 => ... }`), the
// `GeometryOp::Fillet` `edges` field, and in-loop curated-fillet dispatch
// (selector→op build) — landed via #3205 and #4360; the UnifiedDag default
// flip landed via #4362. `single`, `flat_map`, `faces_by_normal`,
// `adjacent_faces`, and `shared_edges` were already landed before that
// (task 2698/2699). This example is NOT a phantom capability gap — it
// demonstrates the v0.1 design vision end-to-end: fillet only the four
// top-perimeter edges via topology-relational selection, rather than
// filleting all edges of the box (which the 2-arg form would do, defeating
// the example's pedagogic purpose).
//
// Real-kernel end-to-end coverage:
// crates/reify-eval/tests/fillet_curated_edges_e2e.rs
// (fillet_curated_edges_3205_e2e) drives this same selector chain
// (faces_by_normal → single → adjacent_faces → shared_edges → flat_map →
// 3-arg fillet) against a real kernel / UnifiedDag scheduler.
//
// Smoke-test coverage tiers in
//   crates/reify-eval/tests/topology_selector_smoke_tests.rs:
//
//   parse               → active    (fillet_top_edges_ri_parses_cleanly)
//   compile-with-stdlib → #[ignore] (fillet_top_edges_compiles_with_stdlib_no_errors)
//                         — see that test's own doc comment for its current
//                         status; do not infer a design gap from this tier.
//   eval (bare MockGeometryKernel) → #[ignore] (fillet_top_edges_evals_to_solid_via_topology_walk)
//                         — blocked on #4727 (pending): all semantic
//                         prerequisites (#3205/#4360/#4362) have landed, but
//                         the bare mock kernel cannot resolve the topology
//                         walk without a real-OCCT-kernel +
//                         set_build_scheduler(UnifiedDag) rewrite; that
//                         coverage is already provided by
//                         fillet_curated_edges_3205_e2e above.

structure def FilletTopEdges {
    let b = box(50mm, 30mm, 10mm)
    let top = single(faces_by_normal(b, vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0), 1deg))
    let top_edges = flat_map(adjacent_faces(b, top), |f| shared_edges(top, f))
    let result = fillet(b, top_edges, 1mm)
}
